 "question": "In both timelines frame 2 is damaged. What does the receiver do with the frames that arrive after it, and which frames does the sender retransmit, in (a) Go-Back-N versus (b) Selective Repeat?",
 "reference_answer": "(a) Go-Back-N: the receiver only accepts frames in order, so it discards frames 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8 (and acknowledges nothing new). The sender's timer for frame 2 expires (timeout interval), it goes back to 2 and retransmits 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8 (then continues with 9); acks 2..7 follow. (b) Selective Repeat: the receiver buffers the correct frames 3, 4, 5, sends NAK 2 (and repeats Ack 1), so the sender retransmits only frame 2. When 2 arrives the receiver delivers 2, 3, 4, 5 in order and sends Ack 5 (cumulative), and the transfer continues with 6, 7, 8...",
